WEBVTT

00:00:00.594 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.971 --> 00:00:06.430
Today, we are talking about two men's styles that clients ask for a lot:

00:00:06.859 --> 00:00:08.990
the classic side part, and the crop.

00:00:09.493 --> 00:00:11.214
The cutting technique is the same,

00:00:11.164 --> 00:00:15.390
but whether it suits or not depends on choosing the right style for the right person.

00:00:15.816 --> 00:00:19.630
A style that looks great in a photo won't necessarily look great on your client.

00:00:19.797 --> 00:00:24.232
We will talk about how to choose a style, the techniques that build it, products,

00:00:24.182 --> 00:00:26.830
and how to teach the client to style it at home.

00:00:27.487 --> 00:00:28.596
The first style:

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:29.716
the side part.

00:00:30.301 --> 00:00:34.996
The top is left longer, longest at the front, and combed over to the side.

00:00:35.503 --> 00:00:36.756
There is a clear parting.

00:00:37.094 --> 00:00:38.196
The sides are short:

00:00:38.465 --> 00:00:41.716
a soft taper, or a fade, depending on the client.

00:00:42.461 --> 00:00:45.876
This style is smart, good for the office and for events.

00:00:46.292 --> 00:00:47.396
But it needs care:

00:00:47.648 --> 00:00:50.276
blow-drying, and a little product every morning.

00:00:50.785 --> 00:00:54.516
The parting can be soft, just where the hair naturally separates.

00:00:54.674 --> 00:00:57.556
Or a hard part, a thin line shaved in.

00:00:58.039 --> 00:01:01.809
A hard part looks sharp, but when it grows back, it gets fuzzy,

00:01:01.759 --> 00:01:03.876
and you can't switch sides anymore.

00:01:04.515 --> 00:01:05.643
The second style:

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:08.203
the crop, also called the French crop.

00:01:08.791 --> 00:01:13.643
The top is short and textured, pushed forward, with a short fringe on the forehead.

00:01:14.152 --> 00:01:15.723
The sides are usually faded.

00:01:16.232 --> 00:01:18.443
A crop is very easy to look after.

00:01:18.789 --> 00:01:23.483
After washing, towel-dry, work in a little matte wax, and you are done.

00:01:23.828 --> 00:01:26.683
It suits busy people, and people who play sports.

00:01:26.975 --> 00:01:29.963
Remember that the top and the sides must be in balance.

00:01:30.071 --> 00:01:35.163
A side part with sides that are too short makes the long top look like a hat sitting on the head.

00:01:35.672 --> 00:01:38.923
A crop with thick sides makes the head look round and heavy.

00:01:39.228 --> 00:01:42.923
So in the consultation, always talk about both parts together.

00:01:43.556 --> 00:01:45.102
So, which style?

00:01:45.414 --> 00:01:46.622
Look at the face first.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.422
For a round face, add a little height on top:

00:01:49.561 --> 00:01:52.782
a side part with some volume makes the face look longer.

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:55.902
For a long face, don't push the hair up too high.

00:01:56.251 --> 00:01:59.742
A short fringe, like a crop, helps the face look shorter.

00:02:00.003 --> 00:02:02.702
Square and oval faces suit most styles.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.142
Look at the ears too:

00:02:04.433 --> 00:02:08.702
if the ears are large, or stick out a little, don't cut the sides too short.

00:02:08.967 --> 00:02:11.182
These are suggestions, not rules.

00:02:11.611 --> 00:02:14.397
In the end, it comes down to what the client likes,

00:02:14.347 --> 00:02:16.382
and you saying honestly what you see.

00:02:17.005 --> 00:02:18.145
Then look at the hair.

00:02:18.598 --> 00:02:20.439
If the hair is thin at the front,

00:02:20.389 --> 00:02:23.425
a side part can sometimes show scalp along the parting.

00:02:23.926 --> 00:02:27.345
A crop pushes the hair forward, and covers thin spots.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:31.105
With a cowlick at the front hairline, the hair stands up there.

00:02:31.454 --> 00:02:34.065
Cut the fringe too short, and it won't lie down.

00:02:34.392 --> 00:02:38.145
Sometimes, parting the hair with the direction of the cowlick is easier.

00:02:38.479 --> 00:02:39.665
Texture matters too.

00:02:40.009 --> 00:02:43.585
Thick, coarse, straight hair holds a crop very well.

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:47.025
Slightly wavy hair gives a side part beautiful movement.

00:02:47.587 --> 00:02:48.954
And ask about lifestyle.

00:02:49.273 --> 00:02:51.594
How many minutes does he have for his hair each morning?

00:02:51.842 --> 00:02:52.794
Does he blow-dry?

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.954
Does he wear a helmet, or a sports cap?

00:02:55.431 --> 00:02:56.554
Something very common:

00:02:56.898 --> 00:02:59.956
the client picks a side part that looks great in the photo,

00:02:59.906 --> 00:03:01.434
but never blow-dries at home.

00:03:01.772 --> 00:03:05.013
A week later, the hair is flat and falls all over the place,

00:03:04.963 --> 00:03:07.034
and the client thinks the cut was bad.

00:03:07.273 --> 00:03:10.234
So suggest a style the client can really do himself.

00:03:10.787 --> 00:03:13.357
Now, the techniques that build these styles.

00:03:13.687 --> 00:03:15.037
First, point cutting.

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:17.987
Instead of cutting straight across in a line,

00:03:17.937 --> 00:03:20.957
you point the tips of the scissors straight into the ends,

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.397
and cut small notches.

00:03:22.826 --> 00:03:26.797
The ends are softer, with movement, and no hard cutting line.

00:03:27.202 --> 00:03:30.717
Then there is texturizing, to remove weight where the hair is thick.

00:03:31.032 --> 00:03:33.597
But with fine, thin hair, go easy.

00:03:33.852 --> 00:03:37.037
Overdo it, and the hair goes flat, and shows scalp.

00:03:37.386 --> 00:03:41.437
And don't texturize close to the roots along the parting, or at a whorl.

00:03:41.785 --> 00:03:43.837
Those short hairs will stand straight up.

00:03:44.443 --> 00:03:47.274
For a side part, the parting must be in the right place.

00:03:47.509 --> 00:03:48.394
Don't just pick one.

00:03:48.793 --> 00:03:50.154
Find the natural parting.

00:03:50.548 --> 00:03:55.354
Wet the hair, comb it all back, then push the top gently forward with your palm.

00:03:55.783 --> 00:03:58.314
The hair will separate by itself at a certain spot.

00:03:58.662 --> 00:04:00.554
That is the client's natural parting.

00:04:00.984 --> 00:04:03.244
Part it there, and the hair lies nicely,

00:04:03.194 --> 00:04:05.674
and the client can easily do it at home too.

00:04:05.932 --> 00:04:09.961
If the client has worn his parting on the same side for years, ask him,

00:04:09.911 --> 00:04:12.314
and look at how the hair is used to lying.

00:04:12.947 --> 00:04:14.234
Then, products.

00:04:14.552 --> 00:04:15.354
In general:

00:04:15.463 --> 00:04:19.034
a matte wax, or clay, gives texture without shine:

00:04:19.214 --> 00:04:20.074
good for a crop.

00:04:20.417 --> 00:04:23.274
Pomade gives shine and a neat, set shape:

00:04:23.543 --> 00:04:25.034
good for a classic side part.

00:04:25.378 --> 00:04:27.674
Water-based types wash out more easily.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:31.514
Sea salt spray is used before blow-drying, for volume and grip.

00:04:32.019 --> 00:04:34.074
For fine hair, choose a light hold.

00:04:34.412 --> 00:04:36.554
Heavy products make fine hair go flat.

00:04:36.815 --> 00:04:37.994
And use only a little:

00:04:38.292 --> 00:04:42.154
take a little on your fingertip, and rub it evenly between your palms first.

00:04:42.579 --> 00:04:47.139
Read the product's instructions, and ask whether the client has a sensitive scalp,

00:04:47.089 --> 00:04:48.074
or any allergies.

00:04:48.642 --> 00:04:50.643
Finally, and very important:

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.963
teach the client to style it at home.

00:04:53.304 --> 00:04:55.123
As you style, talk him through it:

00:04:55.427 --> 00:04:59.763
which direction to blow-dry, how much product to take, how to work it in.

00:05:00.101 --> 00:05:04.883
Hand him the dryer, or the wax, and let him try it once, right there in the chair.

00:05:05.232 --> 00:05:09.454
If the client can do it himself, he will love that haircut for a whole month,

00:05:09.404 --> 00:05:10.483
not just for a day.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.323
Tell him what to avoid, too.

00:05:12.566 --> 00:05:15.043
Too much wax makes the hair greasy and heavy.

00:05:15.392 --> 00:05:18.883
And a side part left to dry naturally usually goes flat at the front.

00:05:19.397 --> 00:05:24.166
So you see, a great men's style is one that suits the face, suits the hair,

00:05:24.116 --> 00:05:25.927
and suits the client's life.

00:05:26.429 --> 00:05:31.607
In the practice lesson, we will cut a side part and a crop, step by step, together.

00:05:31.952 --> 00:05:34.887
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.

00:05:35.141 --> 00:05:36.007
See you next time.
